# LastRunInfo.html after local run

## Trigger (must)

When a script **starts or finishes** local dev execution and assigns ports (`_dev-ports.ps1`, range **5320–5329**), it **must** create or update **`LastRunInfo.html`** at the **repository root** (same folder as `_dev-ports.ps1`).

Applies to at least:

- `_run-all-local.ps1`
- `_build-all-projects.ps1` when `-SkipDevServers` is **not** set (dev terminals spawned)
- Any new “run all local” / dev orchestrator scripts

## Content (must)

Single HTML file, UTF-8 **without BOM**, **no CDN** (inline CSS only; `prefers-color-scheme` for light/dark). Page `lang="fa"` and `dir="rtl"`.

Three sections, each a **table**:

| Section (heading) | Columns |
|-------------------|---------|
| **نتیجه اجرا** | مرحله / وضعیت / جزئیات (build, test, analyze, process start, health check) |
| **آدرس‌های سرویس** | سرویس / آدرس / توضیح (URLs, `pid`, or «بدون HTTP») |
| **تخصیص پورت‌ها** | نام / پورت / کاربرد (from `$script:KaraviDevPorts`) |

## Implementation (must)

- Use `Write-KaraviLastRunInfoHtml` in `_last-run-info.ps1` (dot-source `_dev-ports.ps1` if needed).
- Persian UI strings live in `_last-run-info.template.html` (UTF-8, no BOM); PowerShell fills `__PLACEHOLDER__` tokens.
- Write the file in a **`finally`** block so partial failures still update the report.
- On overall failure, set overall status to ناموفق but still list completed steps.

## Git

`LastRunInfo.html` is generated output; keep it in `.gitignore` unless the user explicitly commits run reports.
